{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02225",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.79,
      "end_seconds": 4.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Morning, doctor. Lovely to meet you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.76,
      "end_seconds": 9.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.34,
      "end_seconds": 18.57,
      "duration_seconds": 7.23,
      "text": "Morning, you know, doctor. I'll stay and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.26,
      "end_seconds": 21.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 23.52,
      "end_seconds": 32.98,
      "duration_seconds": 9.46,
      "text": "So, uh, doctor, it's electric shock pains in my cheek. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.1,
      "end_seconds": 35.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "So, since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.03,
      "end_seconds": 42.89,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "About... well, two weeks. I told my wife I'd come today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.92,
      "end_seconds": 47.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Would you say mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.78,
      "end_seconds": 50.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Mild, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.37,
      "end_seconds": 53.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "How frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.15,
      "end_seconds": 57.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "I'd say all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.79,
      "end_seconds": 64.81,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 64.91,
      "end_seconds": 70.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.21,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.08,
      "end_seconds": 74.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.63,
      "end_seconds": 84.28,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything. What about being afraid to eat, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.37,
      "end_seconds": 88.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Yes, for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.82,
      "end_seconds": 93.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.79,
      "end_seconds": 100.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "Well, I'd give it a five, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.22,
      "end_seconds": 103.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Have you had any hearing loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.96,
      "end_seconds": 112.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.49,
      "text": "Nope, no hearing loss. There was pain lasting seconds, yes, but that went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.24,
      "end_seconds": 118.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Right, any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.09,
      "end_seconds": 121.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.71,
      "end_seconds": 128.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.27,
      "end_seconds": 138.01,
      "duration_seconds": 7.74,
      "text": "Yes, tramadol. I get vomiting. I'm allergic to milk, I get stomach cramps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.65,
      "end_seconds": 148.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Alright, anything in your past medical history I should know? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.36,
      "end_seconds": 158.11,
      "duration_seconds": 7.75,
      "text": "Yes, eczema. Hmm, I've had an irregular heartbeat for nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.31,
      "end_seconds": 166.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.21,
      "text": "So, yes, an irregular heartbeat is known to us, good to have that clear. How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.66,
      "end_seconds": 171.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.72,
      "end_seconds": 174.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.1,
      "end_seconds": 178.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.96,
      "end_seconds": 181.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Do you do any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.64,
      "end_seconds": 185.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.99,
      "end_seconds": 188.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 190.02,
      "end_seconds": 197.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.57,
      "text": "He is on paracetamol, 1 gram, when needed, I give it to him."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.18,
      "end_seconds": 199.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Is that long-standing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 201.5,
      "end_seconds": 203.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "For six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.84,
      "end_seconds": 207.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 208.94,
      "end_seconds": 212.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "No, I've never been operated on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.55,
      "end_seconds": 217.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.91,
      "end_seconds": 225.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "Hmm, my uncle has high cholesterol. My father has Parkinson's disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.36,
      "end_seconds": 229.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.3,
      "end_seconds": 232.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.64,
      "end_seconds": 235.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Right, breathe out slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.03,
      "end_seconds": 259.12,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Touching the right cheek sets off the pain and the face muscles work normally."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.98,
      "end_seconds": 262.68,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.19,
      "end_seconds": 267.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.42,
      "end_seconds": 286.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "Taking everything into account, this is probably trigeminal neuralgia. I can't rule out a dental problem yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.81,
      "end_seconds": 291.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.19,
      "end_seconds": 317.48,
      "duration_seconds": 24.29,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's trigeminal neuralgia, and we'll know more once the an MRI scan of the head is back. Stop me if I've got anything wrong. You've had electric shock pains in your cheek for two weeks, mild, and no hearing loss."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 318.21,
      "end_seconds": 318.91,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.58,
      "end_seconds": 361.13,
      "duration_seconds": 32.55,
      "text": "I'm sending you for an MRI scan of the head because of facial pain. The treatment will be carbamazepine, 100 milligrams, twice a day, titrate. You take it by mouth. It's for nerve pain. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Avoid known triggers and eat soft foods when it flares. Let's get you seen by the neurology clinic, I'll arrange the letter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.9,
      "end_seconds": 365.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.07,
      "text": "Sure, um, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.92,
      "end_seconds": 374.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "We'll catch up in four weeks. So, that's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.82,
      "end_seconds": 380.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Good, uh, thanks, I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}